  "narration_lines": [
    {
      "id": "L1",
      "beat": "B1_HOOK",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 0.08,
      "t1": 3.45,
      "text": "If a bullet hits your vest, you don't fly backward, you barely budge."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "beat": "B2_MOMENTUM",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 3.62,
      "t1": 8.40,
      "text": "Movies send heroes crashing through glass, yet a bullet carries less momentum than a fastball."
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "beat": "B3_KEVLAR",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 8.65,
      "t1": 14.85,
      "text": "Instead, woven golden Kevlar catches the spinning bullet like a trampoline, spreading that force across your whole chest."
    },
    {
      "id": "L4",
      "beat": "B4_CERAMIC",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 15.15,
      "t1": 20.85,
      "text": "For faster rifle rounds, a ceramic plate shatters the metal tip to dust, while Dyneema traps every shard."
    },
    {
      "id": "L5",
      "beat": "B5_NEWTON",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 21.15,
      "t1": 25.85,
      "text": "And Newton's Third Law seals it, any shot strong enough to launch you would launch the shooter too."
    },
    {
      "id": "L6",
      "beat": "B6_FINAL",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 26.15,
      "t1": 29.85,
      "text": "So real armor never sends you flying, it just leaves one brutal bruise."
    }
  ],
